WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.019
Suppose a product price is negative It may be
tempting to use ABS

00:00:06.032 --> 00:00:13.038
and make it positive But that silently invents a
correction The

00:00:13.051 --> 00:00:18.556
negative value is evidence that something went wrong
A safer workflow

00:00:18.582 --> 00:00:23.806
flags the value preserves the source and corrects it
only when reliable evidence identifies the

00:00:23.819 --> 00:00:29.688
intended price This principle applies to dates phone
numbers emails

00:00:29.859 --> 00:00:31.649
categories and other fields
